description
  Test: lexically valid but syntactically wrong.
  Every token here is legal, so the scanner should report no errors.
  The mistakes are grammar mistakes (wrong order, an unsupported type,
  an uppercase keyword, a <= operator our subset does not have), which
  the parser in Deliverable 2 must catch. Reuse this file then.
*/
import "scl.h"
implementations
function main return type double is
variables
    define x of type double
begin
    SET x = 5
    set = x 5
    if x <= 3 then
    display x x x
    endfun
endif main

// EXPECT: none
